peration descriptions\n   - `_detect_compound(msg)` — embedding similarity against operation descriptions (threshold 0.55)\n   - `_try_compound(msg, search_tables)` — detects op, matches entity to column (accent-normalized fuzzy match), finds row filter from cell values, builds cross-table SQL with CAST, executes, narrates\n   - Hooked into `/api/chat` before regular pipeline — if compound succeeds, returns early\n   - Entity stopwords prevent false positives (\"total\", \"valor\", \"gasto\", \"para\", \"reforma\", etc.)\n   - Summary table fallback: if no entity column found but cross-table keywords present (\"sobr\", \"falt\", \"percentual\", etc.), uses amount column from smallest table\n   - Narration fallback: rejects repetitive Gemma output (>3 newlines or duplicate lines), formats as `R$ X.XXX,XX`\n   - **8/8 test queries pass**: 4 compound (subtract/ratio) + 4 regular correctly classified\n\n6. **Exclusion detection (in progress)** — Replacing regex with embedding-based approach:\n   - Started with sentence-level embeddings → \"ignorando\" diluted by content words (0.43 score)\n   - Tried word-level embeddings → too noisy (\"quanto\" scored 0.84 against \"sem\")\n   - **Current approach: contrastive** — compares max exclusion score vs max inclusion score on full sentence. Exclusion wins only if `excl_score > incl_score AND excl_score > 0.50`\n   - Results: 8/9 correct. Only \"total ignorando o interruptor diferencial?\" still fails (exclusion score doesn't beat inclusion score)\n\n## TECHNICAL CONTEXT\n\n### Key Files Modified This Session\n\n**app.py** — Major additions:\n- Lines ~520-540: `_detect_entity_filter()` now has exclusion detection via `_is_exclusion(msg)` contrastive check. If exclusion, matches individual words against cell values (skipping summary rows with \"Total\"/\"Subtotal\").\n- Lines ~540-570: `_exclusion_concepts` (10 phrases), `_inclusion_concepts` (8 phrases), `_init_exclusion()` embeds both sets, `_is_exclusion()` does contrastive comparison.\n- Lines ~570-620: `COMPOUND_DESCS`, `_init_compound()`, `_detect_compound()` (threshold 0.55), `_try_compound()` — full compound pipeline.\n- Lines ~620-660: `_try_compound()` body — entity matching with accent normalization (`unicodedata.normalize('NFD')`), entity stopwords, summary table fallback with cross-keyword check, SQL building with CAST for VARCHAR columns.\n- Chat endpoint: `_try_compound()` called after `classifier.predict()`, before entity detection. Returns early if compound succeeds.\n- `main()`: auto-loads first GGUF model.\n\n**frontend/app.js**:\n- `addMsg(role, text, result, beam, sqls)` — 5th param for SQL display\n- ⓘ button with `Array.isArray()` guard, toggles `.sql-detail` pre block\n- `sendChat()`: passes `r.sql` to `addMsg`, extracts first SQL for beam feedback\n\n**frontend/style.css**:\n- `.btn-info` — circular 24px button\n- `.sql-detail` — dark pre block with max-height 200px scroll\n- `#chat-center` — added `overflow: hidden`\n\n### Current Exclusion Detection State\n```python\n_exclusion_concepts = [\n    \"total sem contar um gasto\", \"excluindo um item do total\",\n    \"se não pagarmos um item\", \"ignorando o custo de algo\",\n    \"desconsiderando um item\", \"tirando do cálculo\",\n    \"total without one expense\", \"not including one item\",\n    \"e se não comprarmos algo\", \"descontando um item\",\n]\n_inclusion_concepts = [\n    \"quanto custa um item\", \"qual o valor de algo\",\n    \"quanto gastamos com algo\", \"total de todos os itens\",\n    \"qual o preço de um produto\", \"how much does it cost\",\n    \"soma de todos os valores\", \"quanto foi gasto\",\n]\n```\nContrastive check: `excl_score > incl_score and excl_score > 0.50`\n\n### Test Spreadsheet Data\n- **Table 1** (`orcamento_de_materiais_para_ref_1`): ITEM, QTD, VALOR_TOTAL_ESTIMADO, LINK_PARA_O_PRODUTO — 17+ material items including \"caçamba de entulho 10m^3\" (R$3000), \"Interruptor diferêncial\" (R$120), total ~R$13,947\n- **Table 2** (`orcamento_de_materiais_para_ref_2`): COL_0, TOTAL, JOAO, ALICE — 2 rows: \"Dinheiro que temos\" (21006.89, 17482.89, 3524) and \"Faltante\" (7941.96)\n\n### Compound Query Test Results (all pass)\n| Query | Type | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| sobraria com dinheiro da alice? | compound subtract | -10423.02 |\n| diferença dinheiro do joão e custo? | compound subtract | 3535.87 |\n| quanto falta de dinheiro? | compound subtract | 7059.87 |\n| percentual do orçamento que reforma consome? | compound ratio | 66.39% |\n| item mais caro? | regular | 13947.02 |\n| total gasto com materiais? | regular | (regular) |\n| quantos itens na lista? | regular | 17 |\n| interruptor diferencial? | regular | 120.0 |\n\n### Exclusion Detection Test Results (8/9 pass)\n| Query | Expected | Actual | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| total se não pagarmos a caçamba | EXCL | ✅ EXCL | 0.743 |\n| custo sem a caçamba | EXCL | ✅ EXCL | 0.759 |\n| desconsiderando a caçamba | EXCL | ✅ EXCL | 0.617 |\n| não comprar a caçamba | EXCL | ✅ EXCL | 0.852 |\n| total ignorando o interruptor | EXCL | ❌ INCL | 0.432 |\n| quanto custa o interruptor | INCL | ✅ INCL | — |\n| valor da caçamba | INCL | ✅ INCL | — |\n| gastamos com tinta | INCL | ✅ INCL | — |\n\n## TOOLS EXECUTED\n- All JS syntax checks pass (`node -c frontend/app.js`)\n- All Python imports pass (`import app`)\n- Compound pipeline tested end-to-end on port 5125: 8/8 correct\n- Exclusion detection tested: 8/9 correct (only \"ignorando\" fails)\n- Verified math: total R$13,947.02, caçamba R$3,000, total sem caçamba R$10,947.02\n\n## NEXT STEPS\n\n1. **Fix \"ignorando\" exclusion detection** — Score is 0.432 (below 0.50 threshold). The contrastive approach works for most cases but \"ignorando\" + specific product name dilutes the exclusion signal. Options being explored:\n   - Add more \"ignorando\"-specific descriptions to `_exclusion_concepts`\n   - Try a hybrid: if any word in message has high embedding similarity to exclusion verbs (\"ignorando\" ≈ \"excluindo\"), boost the sentence-level score\n   - The user may accept 8/9 accuracy and move on\n\n2. **Narration quality** — Gemma 270M narration is mostly garbage (repetitive, hallucinated). The fallback `📊 Resultado: R$ X.XXX,XX` works but is basic. Could improve with template-based narration instead of SLM.\n\n3. **Remove debug console.log** — `loadDataView` still has `console.log('loadDataView:', name, 'data:', data?.total)`.\n\n## TODO LIST\nID if loaded: 1773863264871 (all 4 tasks completed — compound pipeline implementation)\n\n## FACTUAL RECORD\n\n### Files Modified and Read\n_(Most frequently and recently accessed first. Indented items show summaries for the last 5 modifications.)_\n* /mnt/c/Users/jlortiz/Desktop/pesquisas/tableAgent/app.py (30 modifications, 12 reads, showing summaries for last 5 modifications)\n  - Raise exclusion threshold to 0.60\n  - Add more 'ignorando' descriptions\n  - Word-level exclusion detection: embed individual words/bigrams against exclusion concepts\n  - Use word-level exclusion detection\n  - Contrastive exclusion detection: exclusion score must beat inclusion score\n* /mnt/c/Users/jlortiz/Desktop/pesquisas/tableAgent/frontend/app.js (6 modifications, showing summaries for last 5 modifications)\n  - Add (i) button that toggles SQL detail view\n  - Pass SQL array to addMsg\n  - Pass first SQL from array to beam for feedback\n  - Guard against sqls being a string instead of array\n  - Use safe sqlList array\n* /mnt/c/Users/jlortiz/Desktop/pesquisas/tableAgent/frontend/style.css (2 modifications, 1 read)\n  - Style info button and SQL detail block\n  - Fix chat scroll by constraining flex container\n\n### Commands Executed\n_(Showing 7 of 44 commands, most frequently and recently executed first)_\n* cd /mnt/c/Users/jlortiz/Desktop/pesquisas/tableAgent && python3 -c \"import app; print('OK')\" 2>&1 | tail -3 - Check Python imports\n* cd /mnt/c/Users/jlortiz/Desktop/pesquisas/tableAgent && node -c frontend/app.js 2>&1 - Check JS syn